{% comment %}
  blocks/badge-highlight.liquid

  One trust badge: an icon, an optional pill, a heading and some text.

  ## The icon has three sources, in order

  Custom SVG code, then an uploaded image, then the theme's icon set. The SVG
  field exists because merchants are given brand icons as SVG and pasting them
  is the only way to use them without an upload losing the ability to inherit
  colour.

  Pasted SVG is not escaped — it cannot be, or the field is useless — and that is
  the merchant's own input from their own admin, the same trust boundary
  Shopify's Custom Liquid uses. It is wrapped in a span rather than inserted
  bare, so a paste missing its closing tag breaks one badge instead of the
  section below it.

  ## The link wraps nothing

  When a link is set, a stretched pseudo-element covers the tile rather than an
  anchor wrapping the content. Wrapping gives a screen reader one link named with
  every word in the badge, and swallows anything interactive added later.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = block.settings

  assign has_link = false
  if s.link != blank
    assign has_link = true
  endif

  capture icon_px
    render 'icon-size', size: s.icon_size, custom: s.icon_size_custom
  endcapture
  assign icon_size = icon_px | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the surface ----

    The alpha goes into the colour rather than onto the element, the same split
    `blocks/card-content.liquid` sets out at length: `opacity` here would fade
    the icon and the words along with the tile they are read against.

    Default 100, so a badge saved before the slider existed paints exactly the
    colour it was given.
  endcomment
  assign background_paint = ''
  if s.background != blank
    assign background_alpha = s.background_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    assign background_alpha = background_alpha | divided_by: 100.0
    assign background_paint = s.background | color_modify: 'alpha', background_alpha
  endif

  comment
    ---- the box ----

    A fixed width and height, because a row of these is a row of tiles and tiles
    that size themselves to their own sentence are a row of different boxes.
    Zero is the off switch and the value a badge saved before this existed
    carries, so those keep sizing to their content exactly as they did.

    `min-` rather than a hard size — see the note in `base.css`. A merchant who
    writes four lines into a 142px tile gets a taller tile rather than text
    spilling out of it.
  endcomment
  assign box_width = s.width | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign box_height = s.height | default: 0 | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the ring round the icon ----

    A frame the icon sits inside, which is what turns a bare glyph into a mark.
    `none` is the default, so every badge already in a theme is untouched.

    The frame has its own size because it is not the icon's: the ring in the
    design is 56px around a 20px glyph, and tying the two together would mean
    growing the icon to grow the ring.
  endcomment
  assign frame_style = s.icon_frame_style | default: 'none'
  assign frame_size = s.icon_frame_size | default: 56 | plus: 0
  assign frame_width = s.icon_frame_width | default: 1 | plus: 0

  comment
    A percentage, so 50 is a circle at any frame size and everything below it is
    a rounded square that stays in proportion when the frame grows. A px radius
    would have to be re-picked every time the size slider moved.
  endcomment
  assign frame_radius = s.icon_frame_radius | default: 50 | plus: 0

  comment
    Frosted, for a tile read against a photograph. Same property, same rule
    shape and same caveat as `blocks/card-content.liquid`: `backdrop-filter`
    samples what is painted underneath, so over a flat colour it has nothing to
    frost and appears to do nothing. Zero by default, so no tile that existed
    before this gains a filter.
  endcomment
  assign backdrop_blur = s.backdrop_blur | default: 0 | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- a border that is a gradient ----

    **Border color** is a `color_background`, so the merchant can hand it either
    a flat colour or a gradient — the same field type the Group block's surface
    already uses, and the only one in Shopify that returns a gradient at all.

    A gradient cannot go through `border-color`: that property takes a colour,
    and a `linear-gradient(...)` handed to it is an invalid declaration the
    browser drops, which renders as no border at all rather than as an error the
    merchant can see. So the two cases take two different routes — a real border
    for a colour, a masked ring painted in `::before` for a gradient — and this
    is the test that decides which.

    `contains 'gradient'` rather than a parse: every gradient CSS can express
    has the word in its own name — `linear-gradient`, `radial-gradient`,
    `conic-gradient` and the `repeating-` forms — and no notation for a flat
    colour contains it.
  endcomment
  assign border_is_gradient = false
  if s.border_color contains 'gradient'
    assign border_is_gradient = true
  endif

  assign classes = 'badge-highlight badge-highlight--' | append: s.alignment
  if s.hover != 'none'
    assign classes = classes | append: ' badge-highlight--hover-' | append: s.hover
  endif
  if frame_style != 'none'
    assign classes = classes | append: ' badge-highlight--framed'
  endif
  if border_is_gradient
    assign classes = classes | append: ' badge-highlight--gradient-border'
  endif

  comment
    The colour scheme is the parent's unless the merchant says otherwise — the
    same control, spelled the same way, as `blocks/group.liquid`.

    It defaults the other way round from the Group block's, on purpose. A group
    is a container and often wants a surface of its own; a badge is a tile that
    sits inside one, and painting it a second scheme puts a rectangle of colour
    behind every item in a row that already has a background.

    That default is also what keeps this setting from changing anything that
    existed before it. This block had no scheme control at all and never painted
    one, so `false` here would have given every badge already in a theme a
    background it had never had — the section's scheme resolved and painted
    behind each tile. Inheriting is the behaviour they have; the picker is the
    new thing, and it is opt-in.

    `nil` rather than `blank` for the unset test: `false == blank` is true in
    Liquid, so a blank check would read a merchant's deliberate "off" as "not
    answered" and silently turn inheriting back on.
  endcomment
  assign inherit_scheme = s.inherit_color_scheme
  if inherit_scheme == nil
    assign inherit_scheme = true
  endif
  if inherit_scheme == false and s.color_scheme != blank
    assign classes = classes | append: ' color-scheme-container color-' | append: s.color_scheme
  endif
-%}

{%- capture badge_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', block: s, declarations: true -%}
  {%- if background_paint != '' -%}--badge-background: {{ background_paint }};{%- endif -%}
  {%- if s.border_color != blank -%}
    {%- if border_is_gradient -%}
      --badge-border-paint: {{ s.border_color }};
    {%- else -%}
      --badge-border-color: {{ s.border_color }};
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    ---- which way the words run ----

    Separate from **Icon position**, because they answer different questions.
    Icon position lays the tile out — glyph above the words, beside them, or the
    pair centred as a column — and until now the text alignment came along with
    it: the row arrangements said nothing, so the words took whatever the
    container was doing. A tile in a right-aligned group came out right-aligned
    with its icon on the left, which is a tile nobody chose and could not fix
    from its own settings.

    `inherit` is the default and emits nothing at all, so every tile already in
    a theme keeps the alignment it has — including the centred one, whose
    `text-align: center` is part of the Icon position: Center layout and is not
    this setting's to undo.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if s.text_alignment != blank and s.text_alignment != 'inherit' -%}
    --badge-text-align: {{ s.text_alignment }};
  {%- endif -%}
  --badge-border-width: {{ s.border_width }}px;
  --badge-radius: {{ s.radius }}px;
  --badge-icon-size: {{ icon_size }}px;
  {%- if s.icon_color != blank -%}--badge-icon-color: {{ s.icon_color }};{%- endif -%}
  {%- if box_width > 0 -%}--badge-width: {{ box_width }}px;{%- endif -%}
  {%- if box_height > 0 -%}--badge-height: {{ box_height }}px;{%- endif -%}
  {%- if backdrop_blur > 0 -%}--badge-backdrop-blur: {{ backdrop_blur }}px;{%- endif -%}
  {%- if frame_style != 'none' -%}
    --badge-frame-size: {{ frame_size }}px;
    --badge-frame-style: {{ frame_style }};
    --badge-frame-width: {{ frame_width }}px;
    --badge-frame-radius: {{ frame_radius }}%;
    {%- if s.icon_frame_color != blank -%}--badge-frame-color: {{ s.icon_frame_color }};{%- endif -%}
    {%- if s.icon_frame_background != blank -%}--badge-frame-background: {{ s.icon_frame_background }};{%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="{{ classes }}"
  data-block-spacing
  style="{{ badge_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <div class="badge-highlight__icon">
    {%- if s.custom_svg != blank -%}
      <span class="badge-highlight__svg" aria-hidden="true">{{ s.custom_svg }}</span>
    {%- elsif s.icon_image != blank -%}
      {% render 'image',
         image: s.icon_image,
         alt: '',
         ratio: 'square',
         sizes: '64px' %}
    {%- elsif s.icon != 'none' -%}
      {% render 'icon', icon: s.icon, size: icon_size %}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <div class="badge-highlight__body">
    {%- if s.pill != blank -%}
      <span
        class="badge-highlight__pill"
        style="
          {%- if s.pill_background != blank %}--pill-background: {{ s.pill_background }};{% endif -%}
          {%- if s.pill_color != blank %}--pill-color: {{ s.pill_color }};{% endif -%}
        "
      >
        {{ s.pill }}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.heading != blank -%}
      <h3 class="badge-highlight__heading">
        {%- if has_link -%}
          <a class="badge-highlight__link" href="{{ s.link }}">{{ s.heading }}</a>
        {%- else -%}
          {{ s.heading }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </h3>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if s.text != blank -%}
      <div class="badge-highlight__text rte">{{ s.text }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.name",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.headers.icon" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.paragraph" },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "icon", "label": "t:blocks.icon_with_text.settings.icon.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:settings_schema.typography.options.case_default" },
        { "value": "truck", "label": "t:blocks.icon_with_text.settings.icon.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "shield", "label": "t:blocks.icon_with_text.settings.icon.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "refresh", "label": "t:blocks.icon_with_text.settings.icon.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "check", "label": "t:blocks.icon_with_text.settings.icon.options__4.label" },
        { "value": "star", "label": "t:blocks.icon_with_text.settings.icon.options__5.label" },
        { "value": "info", "label": "t:blocks.icon_with_text.settings.icon.options__6.label" }
      ],
      "default": "truck"
    },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "icon_image", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_image.label", "info": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_image.info" },
    { "type": "html", "id": "custom_svg", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.custom_svg.label", "info": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.custom_svg.info" },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "icon_size", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_size.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "extra_small", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "small", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "medium", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "large", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__4.label" },
        { "value": "extra_large", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__5.label" },
        { "value": "custom", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.options__6.label" }
      ],
      "default": "medium"
    },
    {
      "type": "range", "id": "icon_size_custom", "label": "t:shared.icon_size.custom.label",
      "info": "t:shared.icon_size.custom.info",
      "min": 16, "max": 96, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 32,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_size == 'custom' }}"
    },
    { "type": "color", "id": "icon_color", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_color.label" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "icon_frame_style",
      "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_frame_style.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_frame_style.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_frame_style.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "solid", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_frame_style.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "dashed", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_frame_style.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "dotted", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_frame_style.options__4.label" }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "icon_frame_size",
      "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_frame_size.label",
      "min": 24, "max": 120, "step": 2, "unit": "px", "default": 56,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_frame_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "icon_frame_width",
      "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_frame_width.label",
      "min": 0, "max": 6, "step": 1, "unit": "px", "default": 1,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_frame_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "icon_frame_radius",
      "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_frame_radius.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_frame_radius.info",
      "min": 0, "max": 50, "step": 2, "unit": "%", "default": 50,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_frame_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "icon_frame_color",
      "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_frame_color.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_frame_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_background",
      "id": "icon_frame_background",
      "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_frame_background.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.icon_frame_background.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.icon_frame_style != 'none' }}"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.headers.content" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "pill", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.pill.label" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "pill_background", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.pill_background.label" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "pill_color", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.pill_color.label" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "t:shared.heading.label", "default": "Free shipping" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "text", "label": "t:shared.text.label" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "link", "label": "t:shared.link.label", "info": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.link.info" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.headers.style" },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "inherit_color_scheme",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.inherit_color_scheme.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.inherit_color_scheme.info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:shared.color_scheme.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.inherit_color_scheme == false }}"
    },
    { "type": "color", "id": "background", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.background.label" },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "background_opacity",
      "label": "t:blocks.card_content.settings.background_opacity.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.background_opacity.info",
      "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 5, "unit": "%", "default": 100
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "backdrop_blur",
      "label": "t:blocks.card_content.settings.backdrop_blur.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.card_content.settings.backdrop_blur.info",
      "min": 0, "max": 40, "step": 2, "unit": "px", "default": 0
    },
    { "type": "color_background", "id": "border_color", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.border_color.label", "info": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.border_color.info" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "border_width", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.border_width.label", "min": 0, "max": 6, "step": 1, "unit": "px", "default": 0 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "radius", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.radius.label", "min": 0, "max": 40, "step": 2, "unit": "px", "default": 8 },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "width",
      "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.width.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.width.info",
      "min": 0, "max": 200, "step": 2, "unit": "px", "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "height",
      "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.height.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.height.info",
      "min": 0, "max": 200, "step": 2, "unit": "px", "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "alignment", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.alignment.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "top", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.alignment.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "center", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.alignment.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "start", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.alignment.options__3.label" }
      ],
      "default": "top"
    },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "text_alignment", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.text_alignment.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.text_alignment.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "inherit", "label": "t:settings_schema.typography.options.case_default" },
        { "value": "start", "label": "t:shared.alignment.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "center", "label": "t:shared.alignment.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "end", "label": "t:shared.alignment.options__3.label" }
      ],
      "default": "inherit"
    },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "hover", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.hover.label", "info": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.hover.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:settings_schema.typography.options.case_default" },
        { "value": "zoom", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.hover.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "lift", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.hover.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "fade", "label": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.settings.hover.options__4.label" }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
        {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:shared.spacing.block_header"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "padding_device",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "desktop", "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "mobile", "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "desktop"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_top.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_bottom.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_left",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_left.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_right",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_right.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_top.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_bottom.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_left_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_left.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_right_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.spacing.padding_right.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.padding_device == 'mobile' }}"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "t:blocks.badge_highlight.name" }]
}
{% endschema %}
